==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpʌ.zl̩d/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-puzzled.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[confused|Confused]] or [[perplexed]].
#* '''1848''', [[w:William Makepeace Thackeray]], ''[http://books.google.nl/books?id=Ql0OAAAAQAAJ&printsec=frontcover&dq=vanity+fair&hl=nl&sa=X&ei=u1HrUo-zAoHs0gWq7YHYBw&ved=0CD0Q6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=vanity%20fair&f=false Vanity Fair]'', Bradbury and Sons, 11:
#*: (...) when the day of the departure came, between her two customs of laughing and crying, Miss Sedley was greatly  '''puzzled''' how to act.
#* '''1920''', {{w|Herman Cyril McNeile}}, ''Bulldog Drummond'' Chapter 1
#*: Once or twice he scratched his head, and stared out of the window with a '''puzzled''' frown. And each time, after a brief survey of the other side of Half Moon Street, he turned back again to the breakfast table with a grin.

